    "whatItTellsYou": "A mean bias line near zero with a tight, random scatter within narrow limits of agreement means the two methods can be used interchangeably. A bias line offset from zero reveals a systematic over- or under-reading; a funnel-shaped spread means disagreement grows with the size of the measurement (proportional error).",
